  "theorem_name": "HaarTypeIIResolutionCompletenessBridgeAndFiniteDepthNoGo",
  "declared_proposition": "For every square matrix A and orthogonal two-dimensional Haar transform Q, B=Q A Q^T satisfies ||B||_2=||A||_2 and ||B||_F=||A||_F. If every row and column sum of A is zero, B has zero constant row and column. Thus the complete nonconstant Haar coefficient matrix is an exact multiscale reparameterization of Type-II dependence, and its square-sum is a sufficient operator bound. No fixed maximum resolution is complete: a 2x2 checkerboard inside one next-scale cell has zero aggregates at every controlled coarser level but a next-scale Haar coefficient and singular value equal to 2a.",
  "mathematical_argument": "Left and right multiplication by orthogonal matrices preserves singular values and Frobenius energy. Zero margins are orthogonality to the constant Haar vector. For the no-go, each row, column, and containing dyadic block sum of [[a,-a],[-a,a]] is zero, while the checkerboard Haar pairing and its only nonzero singular value are 2a.",
